WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.077
Use this checkpoint to connect a requirement with the Spark concept that supports it.

00:00:05.077 --> 00:00:08.927
Large files may benefit from distributed scanning.

00:00:08.927 --> 00:00:12.032
Grouping by a key may require a shuffle.

00:00:12.032 --> 00:00:15.932
A previous-event question suggests the lag function.

00:00:15.932 --> 00:00:20.852
A reusable curated lakehouse result may be stored as a Delta table.

00:00:20.852 --> 00:00:25.007
The explain command helps us inspect the execution plan.

00:00:25.007 --> 00:00:28.927
The goal is not to memorize isolated vocabulary.

00:00:28.927 --> 00:00:33.616
It is to recognize which idea becomes relevant when the requirement changes.
